   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cleaning and Preproccessing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 86,
   "id": "8984afa4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Module to track progress bar\n",
    "tqdm.pandas()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 87,
   "id": "34c58b60",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Reset index\n",
    "df_speeches = df_speeches_raw.set_index(['year','country_code'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Drop session column\n",
    "df_speeches.drop(columns=['session_number'],inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Lowercase the speec\n",
    "df_speeches['speech_text'] = df_speeches['speech_text'].str.lower()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove special characters\n",
    "df_speeches['speech_text'] = (\n",
    "    df_speeches['speech_text']\n",
    "    .str.replace(r'[^a-zA-Z\\s]', ' ', regex=True)\n",
    "    .str.replace(r'\\s+', ' ', regex=True)\n",
    "    .str.strip()\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 88,
   "id": "2b073ac4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "100%|██████████| 11141/11141 [01:46<00:00, 104.64it/s]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Remove stop words\n",
    "stop = set(stopwords.words('english'))\n",
    "\n",
    "def remove_stopwords(text):\n",
    "    tokens = word_tokenize(text)\n",
    "    new_text = [t for t in tokens if t not in stop]\n",
    "    return new_text\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tokenize\n",
    "df_speeches['tokens'] = df_speeches['speech_text'].progress_apply(remove_stopwords)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5064e2ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We decided to process the speeches by doing a lower case, removal of special characters and numbers. After that performing tokenization by removing as well the english stop words.\n",
    "The result is a list clean tokens for each speech."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 89,
   "id": "eeeec22d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "100%|██████████| 11141/11141 [01:12<00:00, 152.71it/s]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Lemmatize\n",
    "lemmatizer = WordNetLemmatizer()\n",
    "\n",
    "def lemmatize_tokens(tokens):\n",
    "    lemmatized = []\n",
    "    for t in tokens:\n",
    "        lemmatized.append(lemmatizer.lemmatize(t))\n",
    "    return lemmatized\n",
    "\n",
    "df_speeches['lemmatization'] = df_speeches['tokens'].progress_apply(lemmatize_tokens)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f65dc087",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The decision of using a lemmatizer is based on creating the best standarization of the tokens. This lemmatizer will treat each token as a sustantive and try to turn plural words into singular (e.g. disasters -> disaster). Also in the future it will help the model to have fewer words to iterate over as the same word in plural and singular are transformed into the same token. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 90,
   "id": "4988cedb",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Determine the length of the speeches\n",
    "df_speeches['speech_length'] = (\n",
    "    df_speeches['speech_text']\n",
    "    .str.split()\n",
    "    .str.len()\n",
    ")\n",
    "df_speeches['tokens_length'] = df_speeches['tokens'].str.len()"
   ]
  },
