  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0b75df1a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Climate change vs energy frequency"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 108,
   "id": "88c58acd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df_cc_vs_re = df_speeches.copy()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 109,
   "id": "d67dba6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Bigrams\n",
    "\n",
    "# Energy\n",
    "re_bigrams = {\n",
    "    # Energy\n",
    "    ('renewable', 'energy'),('energy', 'resource'),('energy', 'crisis'),\n",
    "    ('energy', 'source'),('clean', 'energy'),('sustainable', 'energy')\n",
    "   }\n",
    "\n",
    "# Climate change\n",
    "cc_bigrams = {\n",
    "    # Climate\n",
    "        ('climate', 'change'),('climate', 'crisis'),\n",
    "        # Carbon\n",
    "        ('carbon','dioxide'),('carbon','emission'),\n",
    "        # Other\n",
    "        ('global','warming'),('extreme','weather'),\n",
    "        ('greenhouse','gas'),\n",
    "        ('fossil','fuel'),('gas', 'emission'),\n",
    "        # Natural\n",
    "        ('natural', 'resource'),('natural', 'disaster')\n",
    "    }"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "49261e1d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "We proceed by making a division of climate related topics and renewable energy related topics, only using bigrams because that is what we determined on previous steps. The use of bigrams is more accurate than unigrams to determine the usage of keywords on the specific context."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 110,
   "id": "158f44cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "100%|██████████| 11141/11141 [01:21<00:00, 136.71it/s] \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Count appereances in speeches\n",
    "def count_vs_terms(tokens):\n",
    "    energy = sum(1 for t in make_bigrams(tokens) if t in re_bigrams)\n",
    "    climate = sum(1 for t in make_bigrams(tokens) if t in cc_bigrams)\n",
    "    return pd.Series({'renewable_energy_count':energy, 'climate_change_count':climate})\n",
    "\n",
    "df_cc_vs_re[['renewable_energy_count','climate_change_count']]= df_cc_vs_re['lemmatization'].progress_apply(count_vs_terms)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 111,
   "id": "700550b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "renewable_energy_count     1960\n",
       "climate_change_count      18658\n",
       "dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 111,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df_cc_vs_re[['renewable_energy_count','climate_change_count']].sum()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 112,
   "id": "d656b407",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Determine if a speech has or not energy or climate bigrams\n",
    "df_cc_vs_re['has_renewable_energy'] = df_cc_vs_re['renewable_energy_count'].apply(lambda x: 1 if x > 0 else 0)\n",
    "df_cc_vs_re['has_climate_change'] = df_cc_vs_re['climate_change_count'].apply(lambda x: 1 if x > 0 else 0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 113,
   "id": "29a72d36",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Rate of mentions per speech\n",
    "df_cc_vs_re['renewable_energy_1000_rate'] = df_cc_vs_re['renewable_energy_count']/df_cc_vs_re['tokens_length']*1000\n",
    "df_cc_vs_re['climate_change_1000_rate'] = df_cc_vs_re['climate_change_count']/df_cc_vs_re['tokens_length']*1000"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 114,
   "id": "5af09f5f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Group by year rate\n",
    "yearly_vs = df_cc_vs_re.groupby('year')[['renewable_energy_count','climate_change_count','tokens_length']].sum()\n",
    "yearly_vs['yearly_renewable_energy_rate'] = yearly_vs['renewable_energy_count']/yearly_vs['tokens_length']*1000\n",
    "yearly_vs['yearly_climate_change_rate'] = yearly_vs['climate_change_count']/yearly_vs['tokens_length']*1000\n",
    "\n",
    "# Group by year country\n",
    "yearly_country_vs = df_cc_vs_re.groupby('year')[['has_renewable_energy','has_climate_change']].sum()"
   ]
  },
